<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Validated Mathematics of Biological Form" ;
    skos:narrower <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/yan-vibrio-biofilm-nematic-fountain-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/yan-vibrio-biofilm-nematic-fountain-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/yan-vibrio-biofilm-nematic-fountain-3> .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/yan-vibrio-biofilm-nematic-fountain-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Parabolic Radial Compression Stress Center Peak & Margin Vanishing Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes the parabolic radial compressive stress profile across an expanding Vibrio cholerae monolayer peaking at r = 0 and vanishing at r = R | Variables: r: radial coordinate from colony center; R: expanding biofilm radius; ζ: RbmA/Bap1/RbmC cell-substrate friction coefficient; g: exponential growth rate; h: monolayer thickness; κ = ζ g / (4 h)" ;
    dct:source "Beroz et al. (2018) Nature Physics 14:954-960 Eq. (1) & SI Text" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e93f00e/2019-yan-vibrio-biofilm-nematic-fountain.py#L95-L150>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e93f00e/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_095_vibrio_biofilm_nematic_fountain.lean#L25-L48> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def radial_compression_stress (kappa R r : Int) : Int :=
  kappa * (R * R - r * r)
def radial_stress_nat (kappa r_sq_diff : Nat) : Nat :=
  kappa * r_sq_diff
theorem parabolic_radial_stress_center_peak_and_edge_zero (kappa R : Int) (k0 r0 gap : Nat) :
    radial_compression_stress kappa R R = 0 ∧
    radial_compression_stress kappa R 0 = kappa * (R * R) ∧
    radial_stress_nat (k0 + 1) ((r0 + 1) + (gap + 1)) >
      radial_stress_nat (k0 + 1) (gap + 1)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "σ_{rr}(r) = (ζ g / (4 h)) (R^2 - r^2) = κ (R^2 - r^2)  ⇒  σ_{rr}(R) = 0,  σ_{rr}(0) = κ R^2 > σ_{rr}(r > 0)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-018-0170-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-018-0356-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1601702113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1611494113> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Hertzian Rod-on-Substrate Radial Compression Stress & Critical Verticalization Instability (P(r) = (1/2) ζ g (R^2 - r^2) ≥ P_c(L_cell))" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_095.radial_compression_stress" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_095.parabolic_radial_stress_center_peak_and_edge_zero" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/yan-vibrio-biofilm-nematic-fountain-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Critical Verticalization Radius Onset & RbmA Friction-Loss Control Law" ;
    dct:description "Governs the onset and radial propagation of the verticalization front r_vert(R) = √(R^2 - R_c^2) and proves that ΔrbmA / Δbap1ΔrbmC low-friction mutants remain flat (r_vert = 0) | Variables: R_c: critical colony radius at verticalization onset; r_vert: radius of the central verticalized core; σ_c: Hertzian rod-on-substrate peeling threshold" ;
    dct:source "Beroz et al. (2018) Nature Physics 14:954-960 Figs. 1-4; Yan et al. (2016) PNAS 113:E5337-E5343" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e93f00e/2019-yan-vibrio-biofilm-nematic-fountain.py#L152-L280>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e93f00e/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_095_vibrio_biofilm_nematic_fountain.lean#L59-L79> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def verticalization_front_sq (R_sq R_c_sq : Nat) : Nat :=
  R_sq - R_c_sq
def front_stress_residual (kappa R_sq r_vert_sq sigma_c : Int) : Int :=
  kappa * (R_sq - r_vert_sq) - sigma_c
theorem verticalization_front_onset_and_rbmA_control
    (kappa R_c_sq dr_sq : Int) (rc2 excess2 sub_gap : Nat) :
    front_stress_residual kappa (R_c_sq + dr_sq) dr_sq (kappa * R_c_sq) = 0 ∧
    verticalization_front_sq (rc2 + (excess2 + 1)) rc2 = excess2 + 1 ∧
    verticalization_front_sq rc2 (rc2 + sub_gap) = 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "R_c = √(σ_c / κ),  r_vert^2 = max(0, R^2 - R_c^2)  ⇒  κ (R^2 - r_vert^2) = σ_c,  r_vert(ΔrbmA) = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-018-0170-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-018-0356-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1601702113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1611494113> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Hertzian Rod-on-Substrate Radial Compression Stress & Critical Verticalization Instability (P(r) = (1/2) ζ g (R^2 - r^2) ≥ P_c(L_cell))" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_095.verticalization_front_sq" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_095.verticalization_front_onset_and_rbmA_control" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/yan-vibrio-biofilm-nematic-fountain-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Inverse Cell-Length Buckling Threshold & Cephalexin vs A22 Expansion Law" ;
    dct:description "Explains why cephalexin-elongated cells verticalize at smaller colony radii R_c and form larger verticalized cores than A22-shortened cells | Variables: L: rod cell length; L_0: wild-type rod length (2.1 μm); σ_c(L): cell-length-dependent peeling buckling stress; R_c(L): critical verticalization colony radius" ;
    dct:source "Beroz et al. (2018) Nature Physics 14:954-960 Figs. 2-3; Hartmann et al. (2019) Nature Physics 15:251-256" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e93f00e/2019-yan-vibrio-biofilm-nematic-fountain.py#L285-L385>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e93f00e/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_095_vibrio_biofilm_nematic_fountain.lean#L90-L106> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def cell_length_buckling_product_residual (L sigma_c L0 sigma_c0 : Int) : Int :=
  L * sigma_c - L0 * sigma_c0
theorem cell_length_inverse_buckling_and_cephalexin_expansion
    (k L L0 : Int) (rc_long_sq delta_rc_sq extra_R_sq : Nat) :
    let rc_short_sq := rc_long_sq + (delta_rc_sq + 1)
    let R_sq := rc_short_sq + (extra_R_sq + 1)
    cell_length_buckling_product_residual L (k * L0) L0 (k * L) = 0 ∧
    verticalization_front_sq R_sq rc_short_sq < verticalization_front_sq R_sq rc_long_sq
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "L σ_c(L) = L_0 σ_{c0},  L R_c(L)^2 = L_0 R_{c0}^2  ⇒  r_vert^2(L_cephalexin) > r_vert^2(L_A22)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-018-0170-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-018-0356-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1601702113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1611494113> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Hertzian Rod-on-Substrate Radial Compression Stress & Critical Verticalization Instability (P(r) = (1/2) ζ g (R^2 - r^2) ≥ P_c(L_cell))" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_095.cell_length_buckling_product_residual" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_095.cell_length_inverse_buckling_and_cephalexin_expansion" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "MorphoEval simulation-faithfulness rubric v0.1.0" ;
    dct:description "Weighted 0-100 rubric for the faithfulness of a morphology simulation to its organism and source model; Overall = weighted mean. Each score is a pk:LLMClaimAssessment (ProbKnow rubric-assessment template) of the pk:Claim pkr:claim/morphoeval-<sim> against one dimension (dct:subject the dimension concept, pk:assessmentType morphoeval/<version>/<dimension>) with pk:hasScore = score/100 — an uncalibrated rubric score, not a probability — and a pk:hasVerdict band; the overall score has the rubric itself as dct:subject and is also the pk:weightOfEvidence of the claim." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/rubric.yaml> ;
    skos:narrower <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> .

